# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OPEN CONFIG
# Real values, safe to commit. Loaded via Bun's native process.env (this is
# a tooling script, not a SvelteKit app, so there's no $env module here).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The TaBiThA Cloudflare account id -- not sensitive on its own (an identifier, not a credential).
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=8582954a9e4c6f0259c6236be794d7d3

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS
# Left blank here; real values live only in .env.local (gitignored).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Create as an account token (Manage Account -> Account API tokens, not My Profile -> API Tokens),
# named "Notifications - tools/alerts apply", with the single permission Account > Notifications >
# Edit on the TaBiThA account. Used by apply.ts to reconcile config.ts against the live account.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
